--- Completion 3 ---
<command>
def count_sinks(image_path):
    import Object_Detector_Tool

    detected_sinks = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(
        image_path=image_path,
        labels=["sink"],
        save_object=False,
        saved_image_path="detected_sinks"
    )

    sink_count = len(detected_sinks["sink"])

    return sink_count
</command>

You can use this Python program as follows:

result = count_sinks("/path/to/bathroom/scenery/room5201.ome.gz")
print(result) # Expected output: 1
